# Build output
build/
out/
dist/
*.o
*.obj
*.so
*.a
*.lib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json

# Emscripten
*.wasm
*.wasm.map
simulator/web/public/stipple-core.js
simulator/web/public/stipple-core.wasm

# Golden-image test artifacts. The .rgb fixtures ARE committed; the PNGs beside
# them are generated previews for human review, and the _failed/ directory holds
# actual-vs-expected pairs from the last failing run.
firmware/tests/testdata/_failed/
firmware/tests/testdata/*.png

# IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
slnx.sqlite

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Node
node_modules/

# Python bytecode from tooling/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Probe reports carry a device serial, Wi-Fi SSID and MAC address.
# Share the versions from them, never the file.
device-probe*.md
input-capture.txt
knob-capture.txt

# Vendor binaries pulled for platform analysis. Ulanzi's, not ours.
build/vendor-analysis/

# Ad-hoc device capture scratch files.
knob*.txt
probe-out.txt

# Restore images and raw partition captures. Ulanzi's firmware, and specific
# to one unit - the whole point of ADR 0008 is that each device is restored
# from its own capture. Never redistributed, never committed.
restore/
*.img
*.squashfs
res-*.bin

# Internal planning that is not part of the public project.
#
# The blueprint was written before anyone had hardware and is contradicted by
# docs/research/tc002-platform-findings.md in enough places that shipping it
# would mislead newcomers. Kept here so it is still to hand, out of the repo
# so it is not published. Move it to a private repository if you prefer.
private/

# Copied beside the API page at build time so Redoc can fetch it.
site/api/openapi.yaml

# Assembled locally by 'dev.ps1 site' for a preview. The emulator is not
# published to Pages - it lives at 'dev.ps1 serve', where somebody working on
# the renderer already is.
site/emulator/

# Script previews, generated from real rendered frames by
# tooling/site/build-previews.py. Built in the Pages job rather than
# committed: half a megabyte of binaries rewritten whenever a script changes
# is repository weight for something reproducible in a minute.
site/shop/*.gif
site/defaults/*.gif

# The shop page itself, for the same reason and a better one.
#
# It is generated from scripts/ by tooling/site/build-shop.py and rebuilt by
# the Pages job on every deploy, so committing it bought nothing. What it
# cost was the submission promise: adding a script was supposed to be one
# file and a pull request, and a committed page meant every contributor also
# had to run a Python script and commit a two-hundred-line diff of generated
# HTML - or watch CI fail on a check they had no reason to expect.
#
# CI still runs the generator, because that is what catches a script with no
# `# name:` header. It just no longer demands the output match a file in the
# repository.
site/shop/index.html

# The reference pages, rendered from docs/ by tooling/site/build-docs.py.
#
# Same reasoning again, and the sharper version of it: docs/scripting.md and
# docs/mqtt.md are the documents. Committing a rendering of them puts a
# second copy of the same sentences in the tree, and the moment somebody
# corrects a typo in the HTML the two disagree about which is true.
site/scripting/index.html
site/mqtt/index.html

# Integration scripts that run somewhere else.
#
# A Domoticz or Home Assistant script talks to Stipple over the API; it is not
# part of Stipple and does not ship with it. Keeping one here would invite the
# question of who maintains it against an API that is still moving.
tooling/domoticz/
